cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Residency Is Not Reuse: ReduLink for Encrypted QUIC Object Streams"
message: "If you use ReduLink, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Michél
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6834-4422"
    affiliation: "University of the People"
year: 2026
version: "3.17"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pinkysworld/redulink-deduplex-quic"
abstract: "ReduLink studies reference substitution between cooperating QUIC endpoints through three necessary gates: authorized exact state remains resident, transmitted representation boundaries preserve reusable bytes, and avoided literals exceed record and repair cost. The v3.17 artifact adds a complete public IBM registry-trace analysis, immutable compressed registry-layer pairs, corrected Linux kernel-path completion and first-byte measurements, live-exporter multistream isolation, competing-flow fairness, and CPU scaling through 32 MiB. Results are bounded to the recorded single-stack, single-host conditions and do not claim production deployment or universal compression."
keywords:
  - QUIC
  - redundancy elimination
  - deduplication
  - reference substitution
  - transport protocols
license: MIT
